Every start from the base in executeIn now asks, whatever the pull request. The resume path is unchanged and still asks. personsCommitAtRisk(git, branch) was rewritten: it lists the commits of the task's local branch, and of HEAD when HEAD is on that branch or on no branch, that nothing else keeps (new GitOps.commitsOnlyIn). Kept, so not at risk:
- every branch on GitHub;
- the task branch's former tips on GitHub (new GitOps.formerTips, its remote-tracking reflog). This also ends a false hold the fixer's version had when the person rewrote the branch on GitHub;
- the folder's other local branches, so the card's 'keep it on another branch' now works with `git branch x` alone;
- RUN_UNPUSHED_REF, REBUILD_PENDING_REF, DEPS_BASE_REF and the held dependencies.
Of the commits left, two kinds are not the person's: work in progress, and a merge that holds nothing of its own. The second uses new GitOps.mergeAddsNothing: the merge's tree equals a clean merge-tree of its parents. Where git is older than 2.38, Forerunner's merge subjects decide instead. Anything else, or more than 200 commits, holds the run with heldForCommitRedo(base). That is fail closed: no model call, CHF 0, nothing reset or pushed. Sibling (review non-blocking): undoUnpushedRebuild no longer runs `checkout -B` while HEAD is on no branch past the pending rebuild; the hold then reads that commit. Also from the review: the R-dirtyworktree JSDoc is back above cleanAfterCutShortRun. ADR 0111's w15-tail amendment, capabilities.md and the user guide now cover the third reset, what counts as kept and what the person does. Sibling tests passed before and after: Forerunner's own commit whose first push was refused (no pull request) runs again on Try again, and a dependent task whose first run changed nothing (Forerunner's dependency merge on its branch) runs again. Unit cases of personsCommitAtRisk cover a fresh folder, the person's commit kept or not, Forerunner's own and work-in-progress commits, clean and hand-made merges, a branch rewritten on GitHub, and HEAD on another branch.

